From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:55:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 106/117] Revert "pinctrl: qcom: sm8650-lpass-lpi: force
 runtime suspend across system sleep"

Replaced by the signed version posted by Qualcomm (patchwork series 1215029
v2 for the LPASS LPI pinctrl part, series 1209436 for SoundWire), which do
the same thing (pm_runtime_force_suspend / _resume as system sleep ops);
ours was the armada-os form, carried without its author's Signed-off-by.

This reverts commit 0360d7220529.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
index e33d4360c094f..bc7889c993d05 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -220,7 +220,6 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pinctrl_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
-	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
